  "question": {
    "text": "At present, a firm is manufacturing <math><mn>2</mn> <mn>0</mn><mn>0</mn> <mn>0</mn></math> items. It is estimated that the rate of change of production <math><mtext>P</mtext></math> w.r.t. additional number of workers <math><mtext>x</mtext></math> is given by <math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>dP</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>dx</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>2</mn> <msqrt> <mtext>x</mtext> </msqrt> </mrow> </math>.&nbsp;If the firm employs <math><mn>2</mn> <mn>5</mn> </math> more workers, then the new level of production of items is"
